# Pixel-gate evidence: regenerated in seconds by _ref/check.py, so it is proof
# you re-run rather than proof you store. Keeping it out avoids churning ~40
# binaries every time a part is nudged.
# check.py's default out-prefix is splitext(page)[0], so a page named
# chip.verify-full.html emits chip.verify-full-part.png. Match every fixture
# name, not just the plain *.verify ones — the --full fixtures are the ones the
# kit tells you to prefer, so their evidence is what actually accumulates.
parts/*-part.png
parts/*-ref.png
parts/*-diff.png
assembly/*-part.png
assembly/*-ref.png
assembly/*-diff.png
